{"author":"schacon@gmail.com","body":"Data model brainstorm for local PRs/code review:\n\n1. Branch refs — code field already exists (head:base pair, could extend to repo:branch:base)\n2. Reviewers requested — new Set field \"reviewers\" (list of emails asked to review)\n3. Signoffs — new List field \"reviews\" like comments: {author, at, verdict, body}\n4. Verdict values — enum: approved, changes-requested, commented\n5. Review state — \"review\" ticket state already exists, natural fit\n6. Merged — closed:resolved after merge, store merge commit in meta\n7. Draft — not needed, tickets start as new, move to review when ready\n8. Line comments — skip for now, too complex without a diff viewer\n\nMinimal viable set:\n- reviewers field (Set) — who is asked to review\n- reviews field (List) — signoffs with verdict enum\n- Commands: ti review approve, ti review request-changes \"reason\", ti review --request alice@\n- List filter: ti list --needs-review or ti list --reviewer alice@\n- Already have: ti state review to mark ready, ti code for the branch\n\nOpen question: reviews as a standalone List vs specialized comments with verdict field. Separate List is cleaner for querying \"approved by all reviewers\"."}